        "steps": [
          {
            "description": "Clean the potatoes thoroughly and pierce each one several times with a fork.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Place the potatoes directly on the oven rack or on a baking sheet. Bake at 425°F for 1 hour, or until the potatoes are tender.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "While the potatoes are baking, add the green onions, colby jack cheese, cottage cheese, chives, mayonnaise, salt, and pepper to a large mixing bowl.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Once the potatoes are cool enough to handle, carefully cut each potato in half lengthwise. Scoop out the insides, being careful not to tear or damage the potato skins.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Pass the potato insides through a ricer and add it to the bowl with the cheese mixture. Gently mix everything together until evenly combined.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Evenly divide the potato mixture among the reserved potato skins, filling each one generously and smoothing the tops.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Place the filled potatoes in the refrigerator until you're ready to bake them again. Remove them from the refrigerator 15 minutes before baking.",
            "image": ""
          },
          {
            "description": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Bake the stuffed potatoes for 30 minutes, or until heated through and the tops are golden and slightly bubbly.",
